[orch:err] ### pytorch/pytorch#191839 — [Package] trace_dependencies clears caller profiling callback
[orch:err] - State: `OPEN` · Closing-link from PR: yes · Source: `closing_hash`
[orch:err] - URL: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/191839
[orch:err] - Author: yuyz-cyber
[orch:err] - Labels: oncall: package/deploy, bot-triaged
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] #### Issue body
[orch:err] The analysis below describes a profiling-state leak reproducible on current main.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] > `torch.package.analyze.trace_dependencies()` installs its callback with `sys.setprofile()`, but always finishes with `sys.setprofile(None)`.
[orch:err] >
[orch:err] > If the caller already installed a profiling callback, that callback is lost after both successful tracing and exceptions.
[orch:err] >
[orch:err] > Expected behavior: preserve the callback returned by `sys.getprofile()` on entry and restore it from the existing `finally` block.
[orch:err] 
